Among the options, increased capillary permeability (Option A) is the most likely cause of the edema. In MCHD, chronic inflammation often causes capillary walls to swell and leak, allowing more fluid and proteins to enter the interstitial space. This leakage, combined with reduced albumin levels, exacerbates the edema.

